---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../components/ServiceHero.astro';
import BrandBranchesGrid from '../../components/BrandBranchesGrid.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE, MAIN_PHONE_TEL } from '../../data/branches';
import { mergeCredentials } from '../../data/credentials-schema';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../lib/build-location-array';
import { OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA } from '../../data/business-hours';

const title = "GE Range Repair Los Angeles — Same Day";
const description = "$89 dx waived. GE range repair Southern California, JGB/JB electric, JGS gas, Profile True Convection, Café customizable, Monogram luxury. SmartHQ diagnostic.";
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/ge-range-repair/";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "GE vs GE Profile vs Café vs Monogram, which is my range?",
    a: "Four-tier hierarchy under one parent company (Haier since 2016; GE Appliances Louisville KY). <b>GE (mainstream)</b>, JGB/JB electric, JGS gas, JB dual-fuel; most common mass-market tier. <b>GE Profile (premium)</b>, PGB/PS series with True European Convection (third element behind the fan), Scan-to-Cook QR-code recipes, SmartHQ WiFi. <b>GE Café (premium customizable)</b>, CGB/CHS-series with interchangeable handles in brushed copper / matte black / stainless; pro-style aesthetic; shares Profile's internals. <b>GE Monogram (ultra-luxury)</b>, ZDP/ZGP-series 30–48 inch pro-style + dual-fuel, Statement Collection. Parts are tier-specific, a Monogram control board won't cross-fit a Profile even though they share the same parts warehouse."
  },
  {
    q: "What is True European Convection and how does it differ from standard convection?",
    a: "<b>True European Convection</b> is GE's name for a convection system with a dedicated <b>third heating element</b> (behind the rear fan) that actively heats the circulated air, standard convection just circulates air heated by the main bake/broil elements, so the air cools as it moves. True Convection holds temperature more consistently and gets closer to \"even everywhere\" baking. Common on Profile + Café + Monogram. Service implication: if a Profile or Monogram range is baking unevenly, we check the <b>third element resistance</b> ($160–$280 part) before assuming it's a fan issue. A failed third element lets the range fall back to standard convection, it still works, just not as evenly, which is why customers call saying \"it bakes OK but something is off.\""
  },
  {
    q: "GE range F-codes, what do they mean?",
    a: "GE ranges use an F-code diagnostic system similar to GE microwaves. <b>F0/F1</b>, stuck keypad / membrane switch; a button registers as pressed when it isn't. <b>F2</b>, over-temperature cutout (check venting + door seal). <b>F3/F4</b>, oven temperature sensor open or shorted. <b>F5</b>, thermistor resistance drift. <b>F7</b>, function/selector key fault. <b>F8</b>, touchpad ribbon cable connector. <b>F9</b>, door-lock motor fault (self-clean initiation). We read full code history during diagnostic because rolling F-codes often point to one loose connector rather than multiple parts."
  },
  {
    q: "SmartHQ won't pair my GE range, WiFi module or firmware?",
    a: "Standard recovery sequence: (1) confirm router is <b>2.4 GHz</b>, GE's SmartHQ doesn't pair on 5 GHz-only networks; (2) in the SmartHQ app, remove the range completely and re-add from scratch (device list corrupts post-firmware-update); (3) power-cycle the range at the breaker for 60 seconds between retries; (4) if pairing still fails, the <b>WiFi module inside the range</b> ($160–$260) is the next check. SmartHQ is available on most post-2018 Profile + Café + Monogram ranges with WiFi. We run the sequence during diagnostic before quoting the module."
  },
  {
    q: "Is Hotpoint range serviced here, my range says Hotpoint?",
    a: "Yes. <b>Hotpoint is GE's value-tier sibling brand</b> under the same Haier / GE Appliances Louisville KY parts chain. Many Hotpoint chassis share mechanical parts with GE mainstream, motors, bake elements, oven temperature sensors, door switches often cross-fit. Control boards and front-panel assemblies are Hotpoint-specific. We service Hotpoint under the GE service umbrella in LA, same technician, same parts chain, same diagnostic."
  },
  {
    q: "What does GE range repair cost in LA?",
    a: "Residential diagnostic $89 waived with repair. Bands by tier, <b>GE mainstream</b>: bake element $140–$240, gas surface igniter $120–$220, main control board $220–$360, oven sensor $80–$140. <b>GE Profile</b>: Inverter-compatible control board $280–$440, True Convection third element $160–$280, SmartHQ WiFi module $160–$260. <b>GE Café</b>: Profile pricing plus $120–$240 for customizable handle swap (brushed copper / matte black / stainless). <b>GE Monogram</b>: Statement-collection control board $440–$680, dual-fuel hybrid diagnostic (gas-side + electric-side) commonly pushes total to $600+ reflecting ultra-luxury tier economics."
  },

  {
    q: "Why won't my GE range oven heat?",
    a: "On a GE range oven that won't heat, the cause depends on fuel type. On a gas model, the oven igniter glows but weakens until it can't open the gas valve, so the oven won't fire while the cooktop burners are fine — surface/oven-igniter service runs $120–$220. On an electric model, a burned-out bake element ($140–$240) is the usual no-heat part. When the oven heats but won't hold the set temperature or throws an F-code, the oven sensor has drifted ($80–$140). Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair isolate the oven circuit and test the igniter or element and the sensor before quoting. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "Why is my GE range baking unevenly?",
    a: "Uneven baking on a GE range usually points to the convection system or a drifted sensor. On Profile, Café, and Monogram True European Convection ranges, a failed third convection element ($160–$280) drops the oven back to standard convection — still working, just not evenly, which matches the 'something's off' complaint we hear most. A drifted oven sensor ($80–$140) feeds the control board the wrong reading, and a bake element beginning to fail bakes unevenly before it quits ($140–$240). Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check the third element resistance, the sensor, and the bake element before quoting. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
    {
      q: "Where can I find the official GE manual or warranty information?",
      a: `Our technicians work independently of GE's factory service network - we're often faster and available same-day in Southern California.`
    },
  ];

const schemaJsons = [
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Service", "serviceType": "GE Range Repair",
    "provider": { "@id": canonical + "#org" },
    "areaServed": [
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Los Angeles County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Orange County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Ventura County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Santa Barbara County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Bernardino County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Riverside County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Diego County" }
    ],
    "description": "GE range repair across Southern California, Los Angeles, Orange, Ventura, Santa Barbara, San Bernardino, Riverside. Mainstream JGB/JB/JGS, Profile PGB/PS True European Convection, Café CGB/CHS customizable handles, Monogram ZDP/ZGP pro-style + dual-fuel. Haier Louisville KY parts chain since 2016. Hotpoint sibling-brand coverage. SmartHQ WiFi diagnostic, F-code decoder. $89 residential diagnostic waived with repair.",
    "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "priceSpecification": { "@type": "PriceSpecification", "price": "89.00", "priceCurrency": "USD", "description": "Residential diagnostic fee, waived with repair" } }
  },
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": faqs.map(f => ({ "@type": "Question", "name": f.q, "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a } })) },
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Brands", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "GE", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/ge-refrigerator-repair/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4, "name": "GE Range Repair", "item": canonical }
    ]
  }
];

// Wave 46 (2026-05-21): canonical org schema — HVAC 777 LLC + 4 credentials + hours.
// Closes Wave 35 / Phase 2b-1 gap for brand-combo and price-list pages.
// SSOT: src/data/credentials-schema.ts + src/data/business-hours.ts.
const wave46OrgSchema = mergeCredentials({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HomeAndConstructionBusiness',
  '@id': canonical + '#org',
  name: 'Same Day Appliance Repair',
  url: canonical,
  priceRange: '$$',
  openingHoursSpecification: OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA,
  areaServed: [
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Los Angeles County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Orange County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Ventura County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Santa Barbara County' }, { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'San Bernardino County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Riverside County' }, { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'San Diego County' }
  ],
  location: BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL
});
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <Fragment slot="head-scripts">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(wave46OrgSchema)} />{schemaJsons.map((schema) => (<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />))}</Fragment>
  <div class="call-banner"><div class="wrap"><span>GE range service?</span><a href={`tel:${MAIN_PHONE_TEL}`} class="phone-lg">{MAIN_PHONE}</a></div></div>

  <ServiceHero
    section="brands"
    slug="ge-range-repair"
    eyebrow={"GE · Range Repair"}
    title={"GE Range Repair"}
    subtitle={description}
    heroImageTitle={"GE Range Repair"}
  />


<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <a href="/">Home</a> <span class="crumbs-sep">›</span>
  <a href="/brands/">Brands</a> <span class="crumbs-sep">›</span>
  <a href="/brands/ge/">GE</a> <span class="crumbs-sep">›</span>
  <span aria-current="page">Range Repair</span>
</nav>
  <BrandBranchesGrid />

  <section class="trust-bar"><div class="wrap"><span>BHGS #A49573 · Insured</span><span>Same-day in 7 Southern California counties</span><span>Residential diagnostic $89 · waived with repair</span></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <p><strong>When a GE range fails in an LA home, our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair trace it to a handful of repeat patterns: on gas models, a weak surface igniter ($120–$220) behind a burner or oven that won't light; on electric models, a burned-out bake element ($140–$240); a drifted oven sensor ($80–$140) when the oven runs hot, cold, or throws an F-code; and a main control board ($220–$360 mainstream, $280–$440 on Profile inverter-compatible units).</strong> On Profile, Café, and Monogram True European Convection ranges, the third convection element ($160–$280) is an added wear point behind uneven baking. GE is Haier-owned but still Louisville-built, so common parts arrive in 2–4 days. We service GE ranges across the Valley, the South Bay, Pasadena, and Orange County. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), BBB Accredited.</p>
    <h2>What GE range repair costs in LA</h2>
    <table class="price-table">
      <tr><th>Service</th><th>Typical Range</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Residential diagnostic</td><td>$89</td><td>Waived with repair</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GE mainstream bake element</td><td>$140 – $240</td><td>JGB / JB electric</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Gas surface igniter</td><td>$120 – $220</td><td>JGS mainstream</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Main control board (mainstream)</td><td>$220 – $360</td><td>JGB / JB / JGS</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Profile control board (Inverter-ready)</td><td>$280 – $440</td><td>PGB / PS series</td></tr>
      <tr><td>True Convection third element</td><td>$160 – $280</td><td>Profile / Café / Monogram</td></tr>
      <tr><td>SmartHQ WiFi module</td><td>$160 – $260</td><td>Profile / Café / Monogram post-2018</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Café customizable handle swap</td><td>$120 – $240</td><td>Copper / matte black / stainless</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Monogram Statement control board</td><td>$440 – $680</td><td>Ultra-luxury tier</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Door-lock motor (self-clean)</td><td>$140 – $240</td><td>F9 code resolution</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p class="small">Related: <a href="/brands/ge-refrigerator-repair/">GE brand hub</a> · <a href="/brands/ge-microwave-repair/">GE microwave</a> · <a href="/brands/ge-oven-repair/">GE oven</a> · <a href="/brands/ge-monogram-range-hood-repair/">GE Monogram range hood</a> · <a href="/services/stove-repair/">Range / stove repair (service hub)</a> · <a href="/price-list/range-repair-cost/">Range repair cost</a>.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>True European Convection, the Profile+ signature</h2>
    <p>Ranked by how often our techs see them: the gas surface/oven igniter and the electric bake element lead as the most common no-heat causes, followed by the oven sensor behind F-codes and off-temperature, then the True European Convection third element behind uneven baking on Profile+ units, then SmartHQ WiFi and door-lock service. The main control board, mainstream or Profile inverter-compatible, is the higher-ticket repair we reach last.</p>
    <p>GE's Profile, Café, and Monogram ranges include a <b>third heating element</b> directly behind the rear convection fan. The fan draws air across that element, heating the airflow itself before it enters the oven cavity, so circulated air doesn't cool as it moves, and temperature holds more consistently across racks. This is the "True European" part of the branding. Service implication: when a Profile or Monogram range bakes unevenly, we check the third element resistance ($160–$280 part) before assuming it's a fan failure. A failed third element drops the system back to standard convection, still working, just not evenly, which matches the "something's off" customer description we hear most.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>GE range repair, frequently asked</h2>
    {faqs.map(f => (<details class="faq"><summary>{f.q}</summary><p set:html={f.a}></p></details>))}
  </div></section>

  <section id="book" class="cta-bottom"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>GE range service? Call the branch closest to your home.</h2>
    <p>Same-day appliance repair across Los Angeles, Orange, Ventura, Santa Barbara, San Bernardino, Riverside, and San Diego counties. Residential diagnostic $89, waived with repair.</p>
  </div></section>
</Layout>

<style>
  body { color: var(--text); } .wrap { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; } .wrap.narrow { max-width: 820px; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.4rem; line-height: 1.15; margin: 12px 0 20px; color: var(--black); }
  h2 { font-size: 1.8rem; margin: 0 0 16px; color: var(--black); }
  p { line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .call-banner { background: var(--red); color: #fff; padding: 10px 0; }
  .call-banner .wrap { display:flex; gap: 14px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .call-banner .phone-lg { color:#fff; font-weight: 800; text-decoration: underline; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .hero { background: var(--black); color: #fff; padding: 42px 0 56px; } .hero h1 { color: #fff; }
  .hero .lede { font-size: 1.06rem; color: #d7d7d7; max-width: 680px; }
  .hero .crumb { color: #9a9a9a; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 6px; } .hero .crumb a { color: #c9c9c9; text-decoration: none; }
  .hero-cta { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 18px 0 24px; }
  .btn { display: inline-block; padding: 12px 20px; border-radius: 4px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; }
  .btn-primary { background: var(--red); color: #fff; } .btn-ghost { background: transparent; color: #fff; border: 1px solid #fff; }
  .hero-facts { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #c9c9c9; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .hero-facts li { padding: 6px 0; border-top: 1px solid #222; } .hero-facts li:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .trust-bar { background: var(--red); color: #fff; padding: 14px 0; }
  .trust-bar .wrap { display: flex; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .section { padding: 56px 0; } .section.alt { background: var(--gray); }
  .price-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 14px; background: #fff; }
  .price-table th, .price-table td { text-align: left; padding: 11px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .price-table th { background: var(--black); color: #fff; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; margin-top: 12px; }
  .faq { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 8px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .faq summary { font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; padding: 4px 0; } .faq p { margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .cta-bottom { background: var(--black); color: #fff; padding: 48px 0; } .cta-bottom h2 { color: #fff; } .cta-bottom p { color: #c9c9c9; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; }  .trust-bar .wrap { gap: 14px; font-size: 0.85rem; } }
</style>
